@* SaleDetail.razor — Phase 4.3

   Customer-facing sale detail page at route `/Sales/{Id:guid}`. Reached
   from the /Sales list page (Phase 4.2) by clicking a sale number or the
   View icon. All authenticated users can view this page — the backend
   handler enforces role-based scoping (customers see only their own sales;
   staff see any sale).

   BACKEND CONTRACT:
     - Load: GetSaleByIdQuery(SaleId) → Result<SaleDto>
       - The handler resolves the current user from ICurrentUserService
         server-side and rejects customers trying to view other users'
         sales with a generic "not found" message (avoids leaking that
         the sale exists).
       - Returns the full SaleDto with line items + audit trail.
     - Approve (staff only): ApproveSaleCommand(SaleId) → Result
       - Transitions Pending → Approved. Decrements stock per line.
       - Handler enforces [RequireRoles(Employee, Manager, Admin)].
     - Mark as invoiced (staff only): MarkAsInvoicedCommand(SaleId) → Result
       - Transitions Approved → Invoiced (terminal state).
       - Handler enforces [RequireRoles(Employee, Manager, Admin)].
     - Cancel (staff only): CancelSaleCommand(SaleId, Reason) → Result
       - Reachable from Pending or Approved (NOT Draft — use delete-draft;
         NOT Invoiced — use credit note flow instead).
       - Restores stock if the sale was Approved (stock had been
         decremented at Approve time).
       - Reason is required (3-500 chars; enforced by validator).
       - Handler enforces [RequireRoles(Employee, Manager, Admin)].

   LAYOUT (responsive):
     Desktop / tablet (≥992px): two columns
       Left  (8/12): line-item table + audit trail
       Right (4/12): sticky action panel (status + actions + totals)
     Mobile (<992px): single column, action panel collapses to top

   SECTIONS:
     1. Breadcrumb: My orders → [Sale number]
     2. Page header: Sale number + status badge
     3. Action panel (right column on desktop, top on mobile):
        - Status badge (large, color-coded)
        - Audit trail (created / submitted / approved / invoiced / cancelled
          with timestamps; the Created entry also shows the creator's name
          via AuditByFormat)
        - Staff-only action buttons: Approve (Pending→Approved),
          Mark as invoiced (Approved→Invoiced), Cancel (Pending/Approved
          → Cancelled, requires reason via JS prompt)
        - Totals summary (grand total, line count, total units)
     4. Line items table:
        - Line #, Product name, Quantity, Unit price, Line total
        - Notes: today Gross == Line (no discount/tax yet); only Line is
          shown. When discount/tax modeling is added to the domain, the
          table will gain a Gross column — the DTO already exposes both
          GrossTotal and LineTotal so the UI is forward-compatible.

   STAFF-ACTION UX:
     Approve and Mark as invoiced are direct clicks — no confirmation needed
     because they're forward-only transitions and reversible by cancellation
     (in the case of Approve). Cancel opens a JS prompt() for the reason
     (same pattern as AdminProducts.razor's restock flow) — simplest UX for
     a staff tool, no custom dialog component required.

   ROLE-RESOLUTION PATTERN:
     The _canActOnSales flag is computed in OnInitializedAsync via
     AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync() (NOT via
     ICurrentUserService.IsInRole). The reason: ICurrentUserService in Blazor
     Server resolves from IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext, which is only
     populated during the INITIAL prerender request — it's null when the
     component renders over the SignalR circuit afterwards. AuthStateProvider
     is the canonical source of role info for interactive components.
     ICurrentUserService IS still safe to use inside Wolverine handlers
     (where the message bus sets up its own ambient context) — just not in
     the Blazor UI layer for first-render visibility checks.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All button clicks are async event handlers
     that dispatch commands via Wolverine. The Blazor circuit's anti-forgery
     token is established at circuit start. *@

@page "/Sales/{Id:guid}"
@attribute [Authorize]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Queries.GetSaleById
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.ApproveSale
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.MarkAsInvoiced
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.CancelSale
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<SaleDetail> Loc
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject IJSRuntime JS
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider

<PageTitle>@(_sale is null ? Loc["PageTitle"] : $"{_sale.SaleNumber} — {Loc["PageTitle"]}")</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            /* Layout — 12-col grid on desktop/tablet, stacks on mobile.
                                   Left = line items + audit (wider); right = sticky action panel. */
            .detail-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
                gap: 1.5rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .detail-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1rem;
                }
                    /* On mobile, action panel comes FIRST so the user sees status
                                       + actions before scrolling to the line-item table. */
                    .detail-grid .detail-action-panel {
                        order: -1;
                    }
            }

            /* Page header — sale number (monospace) + status badge inline. */
            .detail-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 1rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            .detail-sale-number {
                font-family: var(--rz-monospace-font-family, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
                font-size: 1.6rem;
                font-weight: 700;
                margin: 0;
                line-height: 1.2;
            }

            /* Status badge (large) in the action panel header.
                                   Color tokens mirror Radzen's BadgeStyle palette so the large
                                   badge and the small inline badge read as the same status. */
            .status-badge-large {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
                border-radius: 9999px;
                font-size: 1rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                min-width: 120px;
                justify-content: center;
            }

            /* Per-status background colors (matching Radzen BadgeStyle semantics):
                                   - Draft     → Base      (gray)
                                   - Pending   → Warning   (amber)
                                   - Approved  → Info      (blue)
                                   - Invoiced  → Success   (green)
                                   - Cancelled → Danger    (red)
                                   rgba values are picked to be readable on both light and dark
                                   Radzen themes — foreground is always the darker shade for
                                   accessibility. */
            .status-bg-draft {
                background: rgba(158, 158, 158, 0.18);
                color: #616161;
            }

            .status-bg-pending {
                background: rgba(255, 152, 0, 0.18);
                color: #e65100;
            }

            .status-bg-approved {
                background: rgba(33, 150, 243, 0.18);
                color: #0d47a1;
            }

            .status-bg-invoiced {
                background: rgba(76, 175, 80, 0.18);
                color: #1b5e20;
            }

            .status-bg-cancelled {
                background: rgba(244, 67, 54, 0.18);
                color: #b71c1c;
            }

            /* Audit trail — vertical timeline of timestamps + actors.
                                   Each entry is one row; rows with no timestamp (e.g. a pending
                                   sale that hasn't been approved yet) are shown muted. */
            .audit-trail {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                margin: 0;
                padding: 0;
                list-style: none;
            }

            .audit-entry {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
                gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
                align-items: baseline;
            }

            .audit-label {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.9rem;
            }

            .audit-value {
                color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                font-weight: 500;
                text-align: end;
                font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
            }

            .audit-value-pending {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-style: italic;
                font-weight: 400;
            }

            .audit-actor {
                grid-column: 1 / -1;
                font-size: 0.8rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                margin-top: -0.25rem;
            }

            /* Line items table — RadzenDataGrid styles are fine, just tune
                                   tabular-nums on the numeric columns. */
            .line-item-money {
                font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
                text-align: right;
                display: inline-block;
            }

            /* Totals summary at the bottom of the action panel. */
            .totals-row {
                display: flex;
                justify-content: space-between;
                align-items: baseline;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                padding: 0.4rem 0;
                border-top: 1px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
            }

                .totals-row:first-of-type {
                    border-top: 1px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
                }

                .totals-row.grand-total {
                    border-top: 2px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
                    padding-top: 0.7rem;
                    margin-top: 0.3rem;
                    font-weight: 700;
                    font-size: 1.1rem;
                }

                .totals-row .label {
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    font-size: 0.9rem;
                }

                .totals-row.grand-total .label {
                    color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                    font-size: 1rem;
                }

                .totals-row .value {
                    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
                }

            /* Cancellation reason panel — shown only when the sale is Cancelled. */
            .cancellation-reason {
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-danger);
                border-radius: var(--rz-border-radius);
                padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
                background: rgba(244, 67, 54, 0.06);
                color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                font-style: italic;
            }

            /* Breadcrumb — same styles as ProductDetail.razor for consistency. */
            .breadcrumb {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                font-size: 0.85rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

                .breadcrumb a {
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    text-decoration: none;
                }

                    .breadcrumb a:hover {
                        color: var(--rz-primary);
                        text-decoration: underline;
                    }

                .breadcrumb .crumb-current {
                    color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                    font-weight: 600;
                    font-family: var(--rz-monospace-font-family, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
                }

                .breadcrumb .crumb-sep {
                    opacity: 0.5;
                }

            /* Sticky action panel on desktop. On mobile it's not sticky
                                   (would consume too much viewport height). */
            @@media (min-width: 993px) {
                .detail-action-panel {
                    position: sticky;
                    top: 1rem;
                }
            }

            /* Action button stack — full-width buttons in a vertical stack. */
            .action-stack {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.5rem;
            }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Back button ──
       Returns to /Sales (preserves any filter state via browser back,
       but we use NavigateTo so the back-stack stays clean). *@
    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToList"]"
                  Icon="arrow_back"
                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                  Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Sales", forceLoad: false))" />

    @* ── Loading state ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["Loading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Error state ── *@
    else if (_loadError is not null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadSaleAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── Not found ──
       The handler returns Result.Failure with a "not found" message for
       both genuinely-missing sales AND sales the caller isn't allowed
       to see (defense-in-depth — never leak existence). Either way, the
       user sees the same friendly message. *@
    else if (_sale is null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["NotFoundTitle"]"
                     Text="@Loc["NotFoundMessage"]"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Warning"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Main content ── *@
    else
    {
        <div class="detail-grid">
            @* LEFT — header + line items + cancellation reason (if any) *@
            <div>
                @* Breadcrumb: My orders / [Sale number] *@
                <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="breadcrumb">
                    <a href="/Sales">@Loc["BreadcrumbSales"]</a>
                    <span class="crumb-sep">/</span>
                    <span class="crumb-current">@_sale.SaleNumber</span>
                </nav>

                @* Page header — sale number + status badge inline *@
                <div class="detail-header" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    <h1 class="detail-sale-number">@_sale.SaleNumber</h1>
                    <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(_sale.Status)"
                                 BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(_sale.Status)"
                                 IsPill="true" />
                </div>

                @* Cancellation reason — only shown when the sale is Cancelled *@
                @if (_sale.Status == nameof(SaleStatus.Cancelled)
                     && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_sale.CancellationReason))
                {
                    <div class="cancellation-reason" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Start" Gap="0.5rem">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="block" Style="color: var(--rz-danger); margin-top: 0.15rem;" />
                            <div>
                                <div style="font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">@Loc["CancellationReasonLabel"]</div>
                                @_sale.CancellationReason
                            </div>
                        </RadzenStack>
                    </div>
                }

                @* Line items table *@
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 0.5rem;">
                    <RadzenDataGrid Data="@_sale.LineItems"
                                    AllowSorting="false"
                                    AllowPaging="false"
                                    Style="width: 100%;">
                        <Columns>
                            <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleLineItemDto"
                                                  Title="@Loc["ColLineNumber"]"
                                                  Width="60px"
                                                  TextAlign="TextAlign.Center">
                                <Template Context="line">
                                    <span style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">@line.LineNumber</span>
                                </Template>
                            </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                            <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleLineItemDto"
                                                  Title="@Loc["ColProduct"]"
                                                  Width="*">
                                <Template Context="line">
                                    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="0.1rem">
                                        <span style="font-weight: 500;">@line.ProductName</span>
                                    </RadzenStack>
                                </Template>
                            </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                            <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleLineItemDto"
                                                  Title="@Loc["ColQuantity"]"
                                                  Width="100px"
                                                  TextAlign="TextAlign.Right">
                                <Template Context="line">
                                    <span class="line-item-money">@line.Quantity.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)</span>
                                </Template>
                            </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                            <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleLineItemDto"
                                                  Title="@Loc["ColUnitPrice"]"
                                                  Width="140px"
                                                  TextAlign="TextAlign.Right">
                                <Template Context="line">
                                    <span class="line-item-money">@FormatMoney(line.UnitPrice)</span>
                                </Template>
                            </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                            <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleLineItemDto"
                                                  Title="@Loc["ColLineTotal"]"
                                                  Width="140px"
                                                  TextAlign="TextAlign.Right">
                                <Template Context="line">
                                    <span class="line-item-money" style="font-weight: 600;">@FormatMoney(line.LineTotal)</span>
                                </Template>
                            </RadzenDataGridColumn>
                        </Columns>
                    </RadzenDataGrid>
                </RadzenCard>
            </div>

            @* RIGHT — sticky action panel: status, audit, totals, actions *@
            <div class="detail-action-panel">
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
                        @* Status badge (large) — at-a-glance current state *@
                        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center;">
                            <span class="status-badge-large @GetStatusBadgeCssClass(_sale.Status)">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="@GetStatusIcon(_sale.Status)" />
                                @GetStatusLabel(_sale.Status)
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        @* Audit trail — list of (label, timestamp, actor) *@
                        <ul class="audit-trail">
                            <li class="audit-entry">
                                <span class="audit-label">@Loc["AuditCreated"]</span>
                                <span class="audit-value">@FormatTimestamp(_sale.CreatedAtUtc)</span>
                                <span class="audit-actor">@string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["AuditByFormat"], _sale.CreatedByName)</span>
                            </li>

                            @if (_sale.SubmittedAtUtc.HasValue)
                            {
                                <li class="audit-entry">
                                    <span class="audit-label">@Loc["AuditSubmitted"]</span>
                                    <span class="audit-value">@FormatTimestamp(_sale.SubmittedAtUtc.Value)</span>
                                </li>
                            }

                            @if (_sale.ApprovedAtUtc.HasValue)
                            {
                                <li class="audit-entry">
                                    <span class="audit-label">@Loc["AuditApproved"]</span>
                                    <span class="audit-value">@FormatTimestamp(_sale.ApprovedAtUtc.Value)</span>
                                </li>
                            }
                            else if (_sale.Status == nameof(SaleStatus.Pending))
                            {
                                <li class="audit-entry">
                                    <span class="audit-label">@Loc["AuditApproved"]</span>
                                    <span class="audit-value audit-value-pending">@Loc["AuditPending"]</span>
                                </li>
                            }

                            @if (_sale.InvoicedAtUtc.HasValue)
                            {
                                <li class="audit-entry">
                                    <span class="audit-label">@Loc["AuditInvoiced"]</span>
                                    <span class="audit-value">@FormatTimestamp(_sale.InvoicedAtUtc.Value)</span>
                                </li>
                            }

                            @if (_sale.CancelledAtUtc.HasValue)
                            {
                                <li class="audit-entry">
                                    <span class="audit-label">@Loc["AuditCancelled"]</span>
                                    <span class="audit-value">@FormatTimestamp(_sale.CancelledAtUtc.Value)</span>
                                </li>
                            }
                        </ul>

                        @* Totals summary *@
                        <div>
                            <div class="totals-row">
                                <span class="label">@Loc["TotalLines"]</span>
                                <span class="value">@_sale.LineItems.Count.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="totals-row">
                                <span class="label">@Loc["TotalUnits"]</span>
                                <span class="value">@_sale.LineItems.Sum(li => li.Quantity).ToString("N0", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="totals-row grand-total">
                                <span class="label">@Loc["GrandTotal"]</span>
                                <span class="value">@FormatMoney(_sale.Total)</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        @* Staff-only action buttons.
                           Visible only to Employee/Manager/Admin (matches the
                           [RequireRoles] on each command). ReadOnly is NOT
                           staff for action purposes — they can view but not
                           mutate. Pattern: compute _canActOnSales once in
                           OnInitializedAsync (synchronously) and use it to
                           gate the entire action stack. *@
                        @if (_canActOnSales)
                        {
                            <div class="action-stack">
                                @* Approve — only enabled when sale is Pending. *@
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionApprove"]"
                                              Icon="check_circle"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Success"
                                              Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                              Disabled="@(_sale.Status != nameof(SaleStatus.Pending) || _isBusy)"
                                              Click="@HandleApproveAsync" />

                                @* Mark as invoiced — only enabled when sale is Approved. *@
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionMarkInvoiced"]"
                                              Icon="receipt"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Info"
                                              Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                              Disabled="@(_sale.Status != nameof(SaleStatus.Approved) || _isBusy)"
                                              Click="@HandleMarkInvoicedAsync" />

                                @* Cancel — enabled when sale is Pending or Approved
                                   (NOT Draft — use delete-draft via /Cart; NOT Invoiced —
                                   credit note flow instead). *@
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionCancel"]"
                                              Icon="cancel"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                              Disabled="@(!_canCancel || _isBusy)"
                                              Click="@HandleCancelAsync" />
                            </div>

                            @* Inline error banner for action failures (e.g.
                               "Not enough stock to approve sale. Product 'X'
                               has 3 in stock but the sale requires 5."). Shown
                               ABOVE the action stack so the user sees it
                               without scrolling. *@
                            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_actionError))
                            {
                                <RadzenAlert Text="@_actionError"
                                             AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                             Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                             ShowIcon="true"
                                             Style="margin: 0;" />
                            }
                        }

                        @* Back-to-list secondary action — always visible,
                           full-width, lower visual weight than staff actions. *@
                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToList"]"
                                      Icon="list"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                      Variant="Variant.Text"
                                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Sales", forceLoad: false))" />
                    </RadzenStack>
                </RadzenCard>
            </div>
        </div>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── Route parameter ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Sale Id from the URL. The @page constraint `{Id:guid}` ensures only
    /// valid Guid strings reach this parameter; malformed URLs hit the
    /// router's NotFound template instead.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Guid Id { get; set; }

    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private SaleDto? _sale;
    private string? _loadError;
    private bool _isLoading = true;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user is in Employee, Manager, or Admin role
    /// (matches the [RequireRoles] on ApproveSaleCommand, MarkAsInvoicedCommand,
    /// CancelSaleCommand). Computed synchronously in OnInitializedAsync from
    /// AuthenticationStateProvider so the action-stack visibility doesn't
    /// flicker on first render. ReadOnly users can view but not act.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _canActOnSales;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the sale is in a cancellable state (Pending or Approved).
    /// Drafts are cancellable via DeleteDraftSaleCommand (handled on /Cart);
    /// Invoiced sales require a credit note flow (not implemented in v1).
    /// Computed from _sale.Status after the load succeeds.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _canCancel =>
        _sale is not null
        && (_sale.Status == nameof(SaleStatus.Pending) || _sale.Status == nameof(SaleStatus.Approved));

    /// <summary>
    /// True while an action (Approve / MarkInvoiced / Cancel) is in flight.
    /// Disables all action buttons to prevent double-clicks.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isBusy;

    /// <summary>
    /// Inline error message for the action panel. Populated when an action
    /// fails (e.g. insufficient stock). Cleared on the next successful
    /// action or on a manual retry.
    /// </summary>
    private string _actionError = string.Empty;

    // ── Lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Compute _canActOnSales synchronously via AuthStateProvider so the
        // action stack doesn't flicker on first render. NOTE: we deliberately
        // do NOT use ICurrentUserService.IsInRole here — in interactive Blazor
        // Server mode, ICurrentUserService resolves from
        // IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext, which is null over the SignalR
        // circuit (only populated during the initial prerender). The
        // AuthStateProvider is the canonical source for interactive
        // components — it reads from the Blazor circuit's authentication
        // state, which is preserved across circuit interactions.
        //
        // The Wolverine command handlers also enforce [RequireRoles]
        // server-side (defense-in-depth), so even if a non-staff user could
        // somehow see the buttons, the handler would reject the dispatch.
        var authState = await AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
        var user = authState.User;
        _canActOnSales = user.IsInRole(Roles.Admin)
                         || user.IsInRole(Roles.Manager)
                         || user.IsInRole(Roles.Employee);

        try
        {
            await LoadSaleAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadSaleAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;
        _loadError = null;

        try
        {
            await LoadSaleCoreAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Silent-reload variant used by ExecuteActionAsync after a successful
    /// action. Skips toggling _isLoading so the page doesn't flash the
    /// full-page loading spinner between a successful action and the
    /// refreshed content. Backported from UserDetail.razor (phase-6.3)
    /// where the same pattern was introduced to fix a P2 soft-issue
    /// flagged in phase-6.3-static-review.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ReloadSaleSilentlyAsync()
    {
        // NOTE: do NOT touch _isLoading here — that would blank the page
        // with the loading spinner. We keep _isBusy = true (set by the
        // caller ExecuteActionAsync) so action buttons stay disabled while
        // the reload is in flight.
        try
        {
            await LoadSaleCoreAsync();
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            // Silent-reload failures are non-fatal — the action itself
            // already succeeded and we already toasted success. The next
            // user interaction (or a manual page refresh) will surface
            // any persistent load failure via the regular LoadSaleAsync
            // path. Logging would be nice but this is a UI-layer catch.
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Shared core for both LoadSaleAsync (initial load + retry) and
    /// ReloadSaleSilentlyAsync (post-action refresh). Sets _sale + _loadError.
    /// Does NOT touch _isLoading — that's the caller's responsibility.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task LoadSaleCoreAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var query = new GetSaleByIdQuery { SaleId = Id };
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<SaleDto>>(query);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                _sale = result.Value;
            }
            else
            {
                // result.Error contains the handler's user-friendly message.
                // For "not found" (covers both genuinely-missing AND
                // permission-denied), we show the same NotFound UI.
                _loadError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
                _sale = null;
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _loadError = Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
            _sale = null;
        }
    }

    // ── Staff actions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task HandleApproveAsync()
    {
        if (_sale is null || _isBusy) return;

        // Defensive: button is disabled when status != Pending, but the
        // handler also enforces this. Belt-and-suspenders.
        if (_sale.Status != nameof(SaleStatus.Pending)) return;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionApprove"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(new ApproveSaleCommand(_sale.Id)));
    }

    private async Task HandleMarkInvoicedAsync()
    {
        if (_sale is null || _isBusy) return;

        if (_sale.Status != nameof(SaleStatus.Approved)) return;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionMarkInvoiced"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(new MarkAsInvoicedCommand(_sale.Id)));
    }

    private async Task HandleCancelAsync()
    {
        if (_sale is null || _isBusy) return;
        if (!_canCancel) return;

        // Use the browser's native prompt() for the cancellation reason —
        // same UX pattern as AdminProducts.razor's restock flow. Simplest
        // approach for a staff tool; no custom dialog component required.
        // The reason is validated client-side (3-500 chars) before
        // dispatching; the FluentValidation validator on the command also
        // validates server-side (defense-in-depth).
        var reason = await JS.InvokeAsync<string?>("prompt", Loc["CancelPromptMessage"], "");

        // User clicked Cancel on the prompt, or entered empty/whitespace.
        // Silent abort — no error toast (the user explicitly chose not to
        // cancel; we don't want to scold them).
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(reason))
        {
            return;
        }

        reason = reason.Trim();

        // Client-side validation: 3-500 chars (matches CancelSaleCommandValidator).
        if (reason.Length < 3 || reason.Length > 500)
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["CancelReasonLengthError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionCancel"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(new CancelSaleCommand(_sale.Id, reason)));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Common wrapper for the three staff actions: sets _isBusy, clears the
    /// previous _actionError, dispatches the command, handles success
    /// (toast + reload the sale to refresh audit trail + status badge) and
    /// failure (inline _actionError banner + error toast).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ExecuteActionAsync(string actionName, Func<Task<Result>> dispatch)
    {
        _isBusy = true;
        _actionError = string.Empty;

        try
        {
            var result = await dispatch();

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActionSuccessFormat"], actionName),
                    summary: Loc["ActionSuccessTitle"]);

                // Reload the sale to refresh the status badge, audit trail,
                // and action-button enabled states. Uses the SILENT reload
                // (not LoadSaleAsync) so the page doesn't flash the full-page
                // loading spinner between the toast and the refreshed content.
                // _isBusy stays true here (set at the top of this method) so
                // action buttons remain disabled during the reload.
                await ReloadSaleSilentlyAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                // result.Error contains the handler's user-friendly message
                // (e.g. "Not enough stock to approve sale. Product 'X' has 3
                // in stock but the sale requires 5.").
                _actionError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericAction"];
                await Toast.Error(_actionError, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _actionError = Loc["Error_GenericAction"];
            await Toast.Error(_actionError, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusy = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Display helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a MoneyDto for display. IRR is labelled "ریال" (no division —
    /// matches Sales.razor so an order's totals read the same on the list
    /// and the detail page). Other currencies pass through unchanged.
    /// </summary>
    private static string FormatMoney(MoneyDto? money)
    {
        if (money is null) return "—";
        var isIrr = string.Equals(money.Currency, "IRR", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        var unit = isIrr ? "ریال" : money.Currency;
        return $"{money.Amount.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)} {unit}";
    }

    // ── Tehran timezone ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Tehran abolished DST in 2022, so a fixed UTC+03:30 offset is
    // functionally equivalent to the IANA "Asia/Tehran" zone for all
    // dates from 2022 onward. We do the offset arithmetic inline in
    // FormatTimestamp instead of using a static TimeZoneInfo field —
    // this avoids (a) platform-specific timezone-lookup failures that
    // were causing the field to be null on some Windows deployments,
    // and (b) Blazor Server hot-reload limitations where static field
    // initializers don't get re-evaluated after a code change.

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a UTC timestamp for display in Tehran time, culture-aware.
    ///
    /// WHY NOT .LocalDateTime:
    ///   .LocalDateTime converts to the SERVER's local timezone, which is
    ///   UTC on this deployment. The user explicitly asked for Tehran
    ///   time, so we add a fixed +3:30 offset (Tehran abolished DST in
    ///   2022) and format the result.
    ///
    /// WHY NOT TimeZoneInfo.ConvertTime:
    ///   We previously used a static TimeZoneInfo field, but it was coming
    ///   back null on some Windows deployments (TryFindSystemTimeZoneById
    ///   edge cases + Blazor hot-reload doesn't refresh static field
    ///   initializers). Inline arithmetic is bulletproof — no timezone
    ///   lookup, no static state.
    ///
    /// Format string "g" = short date + short time (culture-dependent).
    /// For fa-IR with the PersianCalendar configured, this renders as
    /// e.g. "۱۴۰۳/۰۵/۱۲ ۱۵:۳۰" (Jalali date + Persian-digit time).
    /// For en-US it renders as e.g. "8/2/2024 3:30 PM".
    /// </summary>
    private static string FormatTimestamp(DateTimeOffset utc)
    {
        // Tehran = UTC + 3:30 (no DST since 2022). AddHours shifts the
        // datetime but keeps the +00:00 offset; .DateTime extracts the
        // shifted DateTime without any further timezone conversion.
        var tehran = utc.AddHours(3.5);
        return tehran.DateTime.ToString("g", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Maps a sale status string (the SaleStatus enum's ToString() output)
    /// to a Radzen BadgeStyle for color coding (used by the small inline
    /// badge next to the sale number). Same mapping as Sales.razor.
    /// </summary>
    private static BadgeStyle GetStatusBadgeStyle(string status) => status switch
    {
        "Draft" => BadgeStyle.Base,
        "Pending" => BadgeStyle.Warning,
        "Approved" => BadgeStyle.Info,
        "Invoiced" => BadgeStyle.Success,
        "Cancelled" => BadgeStyle.Danger,
        _ => BadgeStyle.Base
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns a CSS class for the large status badge in the action panel.
    /// Uses Tailwind-like inline color tokens (rgba + foreground color) —
    /// same pattern as ProductDetail.razor's stock badges.
    /// </summary>
    private static string GetStatusBadgeCssClass(string status) => status switch
    {
        "Draft" => "status-bg-draft",
        "Pending" => "status-bg-pending",
        "Approved" => "status-bg-approved",
        "Invoiced" => "status-bg-invoiced",
        "Cancelled" => "status-bg-cancelled",
        _ => "status-bg-draft"
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns a Material icon name for the large status badge.
    /// </summary>
    private static string GetStatusIcon(string status) => status switch
    {
        "Draft" => "edit_note",
        "Pending" => "hourglass_top",
        "Approved" => "check_circle",
        "Invoiced" => "receipt_long",
        "Cancelled" => "cancel",
        _ => "help_outline"
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns a localized label for the sale status. Falls back to the
    /// raw status string if no localization key matches. Same pattern as
    /// Sales.razor.
    /// </summary>
    private string GetStatusLabel(string status)
    {
        var key = $"Status{status}";
        var localized = Loc[key];
        return localized == key ? status : localized;
    }

    // ── SaleStatus mirror (for nameof() comparisons) ───────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Local mirror of the SaleStatus enum value NAMES. Used via nameof()
    /// so the .razor layer is loosely coupled to the domain enum (no
    /// using directive on TakOne.Domain.Sales.Enums needed). Keep these
    /// in sync with TakOne.Domain.Sales.Enums.SaleStatus.
    /// </summary>
    private static class SaleStatus
    {
        public const string Draft = "Draft";
        public const string Pending = "Pending";
        public const string Approved = "Approved";
        public const string Invoiced = "Invoiced";
        public const string Cancelled = "Cancelled";
    }
}